course: dictionary
lesson: 1629
title: Proper nouns and place names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chicago is a proper noun. It is the name of one special place, so it always starts with a capital letter. Chicago is a big city in the United States, in the state of Illinois, on the shore of Lake Michigan.
explain: You can learn about a place from the words around it. «The first skyscraper, built in Chicago in 1885, had about 10 floors» tells you Chicago is a place where buildings were built, so it must be a city.
explain: When the context is not enough, check a dictionary. Chicago is the third-largest city in the USA, so it is one of the biggest cities in America, but it is not the biggest.
fact: Chicago is a big city in the United States, in the state of Illinois.
fact: Chicago sits on the shore of Lake Michigan, and it is nicknamed «the Windy City».
fact: Chicago is the third-largest city in the USA.
fact: «The first skyscraper, built in Chicago in 1885, had about 10 floors.»
fact: Proper nouns name one special person, place or thing, so they start with a capital letter.
exercise: What kind of word is Chicago? | A verb, an action word | *A proper noun, the name of one special place | A small joining word, like the | A describing word, like big
exercise: «The first skyscraper, built in Chicago in 1885, had about 10 floors.» In which country is Chicago? | Ireland | Canada | *The United States | Mexico
exercise: What is «the Windy City»? | A weather report from London | *A nickname for Chicago | A type of skyscraper | A windy beach in Dublin
test: In which state is Chicago? | California | Texas | *Illinois | Ohio
test: In the words «a boy from chicago», which word must start with a capital letter? | from | *Chicago | boy | a
exam: What does «third-largest» mean for Chicago? | Third city from the top of a map | Third oldest city in the USA | *Third biggest in size among cities in the USA | Third most visited park in the USA
